Report nested functions that only reference a more distant ancestor, matching Unicorn. For example, `inner` below was previously allowed and now reports that it can move to the outer scope:

```js
const shared = 1;
function outer() {
    function inner() {
        return shared;
    }
    return inner();
}
```

Include parameter defaults in capture checks so functions that depend on parent variables or lexical `this` remain nested. Preserve captures in parents with direct eval and Unicorn's handling of variables used directly by the parent. Cache each ancestor symbol's referencing scopes once per file, shared across candidate functions.

Fixes #26591

Pure refactor.

My spate of refactoring PRs introduced a lot of `use super::super::...;` statements in pipeline modules. In some cases this expanded to `use super::super::super::...;` which is just silly.

Switch to import paths which start at crate root and work down, instead of working up from the importer. This makes it clearer what the import target is.

```rust
// Before
use super::super::super::bitmap::bm_set;
// After
use crate::pipeline::bitmap::bm_set;
```

Pure refactor. No alteration to code, just moving code around.

Move the 2 lookup tables used by `classify` out of `Tables` and into 2 separate structs.

Before:

```rust
struct Tables {
    pub mrg_lo: [u8; 16],
    pub mrg_hi: [u8; 16],
    pub mrg_lo_ts: [u8; 16],
    pub wb_lo: [u8; 16],
    pub wb_hi: [u8; 16],
    // ...
}
```

After:

```rust
struct Tables {
    pub merged_luts: MergedLuts,
    pub word_luts: WordLuts,
    // ...
}

struct MergedLuts {
    pub lo: [u8; 16],
    pub hi: [u8; 16],
    pub lo_ts: [u8; 16],
}

pub struct WordLuts {
    pub lo: [u8; 16],
    pub hi: [u8; 16],
}
```

Move these types and associated code into a new `classify_luts.rs` file.

Refactor.

Introduce a macro `matches_tk!` which allows checking a `u8` against various `TokenKind`s' discriminants.

```rust
// Before
if matches!(kind, tk!(Ident) | tk!(PrivateIdent)) { /* ... */ }
// After
if matches_tk!(kind, Ident | PrivateIdent) { /* ... */ }
```

Additionally, expand the role of existing `tk!` macro to make it produce `|` patterns.

```rust
// Before
match kind {
    tk!(Number) | tk!(BigInt) | tk!(String) | tk!(RegExp) => do_something(),
    _ => do_something_else(),
}

// After
match kind {
    tk!(Number | BigInt | String | RegExp) => do_something(),
    _ => do_something_else(),
}
```

Both are shorter, and easier to read.

Use `matches_tk!` macro to shorten some code in `compress`.
